
"smart_sources:node_modules/typed-query-selector/README.md": {"path":"node_modules/typed-query-selector/README.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1eemgkg","at":1770841336274},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1766770955285,"size":9437,"at":1770841336428,"hash":"1eemgkg"},"blocks":{"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`":[1,266],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#{1}":[3,5],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💿 Install":[6,11],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💿 Install#{1}":[8,11],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🍉 Usage":[12,121],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🍉 Usage#Automatic shim":[14,60],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🍉 Usage#Automatic shim#{1}":[16,60],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🍉 Usage#Strict mode":[61,90],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🍉 Usage#Strict mode#{1}":[63,90],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🍉 Usage#Use the parser":[91,121],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🍉 Usage#Use the parser#{1}":[93,121],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases":[122,247],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#With class, ID, pseudo class or attribute":[124,163],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#With class, ID, pseudo class or attribute#{1}":[126,163],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Combinators":[164,179],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Combinators#{1}":[166,179],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Grouping selectors":[180,189],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Grouping selectors#{1}":[182,189],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Fallback":[190,247],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Fallback#Custom Elements":[192,223],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Fallback#Custom Elements#{1}":[194,223],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Fallback#Invalid selector":[224,247],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#💡 Supported Use Cases#Fallback#Invalid selector#{1}":[226,247],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🔩 Technical Details":[248,256],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🔩 Technical Details#Why returns `never` in strict mode?":[250,256],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🔩 Technical Details#Why returns `never` in strict mode?#{1}":[252,256],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🔗 Related":[257,260],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#🔗 Related#{1}":[259,260],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#📃 License":[261,266],"#🏷 Typed `querySelector`#📃 License#{1}":[263,266]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Playground","target":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#","line":33},{"title":"Playground","target":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBDAnmApnA3gXzgMyhEOAciVQBMBaARwFcUpEKBnFAGxQGMZoiAoXshA40QKAHYwAdLXqIAym07coACiJlgANwDEAQzBgiASjgB6U3AC8lgHxwAEgBUAsgBkAIloCi7URKA","line":46},{"title":"test') // return `never`\n```\n\nThis feature won't be enabled by default and you can opt-in.\nIf you want to enable this, change import entry:\n\n```diff\n- import 'typed-query-selector'\n+ import 'typed-query-selector/strict'\n```\n\nThat's all. If you pass an invalid selector,\nbecause it returns `never`, TypeScript will prevent you from\naccessing properties/methods on element or using element at somewhere.\n\nNote that it doesn't guarantee that it can detect every kind of syntax errors,\nsince such parser will become very complex and compilation performance may go bad.\n\n### Use the parser\n\nIf you just want to use the selector parser itself, we've exported for you:\n\n```typescript\nimport type {\n  ParseSelector,\n  StrictlyParseSelector, // or use the strict parser\n} from 'typed-query-selector/parser'\n\ntype MyElement = ParseSelector<'form#login'>\n```\n\n_[Playground","target":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBDAnmApnA3nACgQygZxQGUUAbFAYxmjgF84AzKCEOAciVQBMBaARwCuKKIh6FyVaAHoweQlDYAoRZzQBZRAFFyIFADt4AXmxziZStSgAeNg2ggAxKQgBzYHrYA+IA","line":73},{"title":"Playground","target":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBDAnmApnA3nACgQygZxQGUUAbFAYxmjgF84AzKCEOAciVQBMBaARwCuKKIh6FyVaAHoweQlDYAoRZzQBZRAFFyIFADt4AXmxziZStSgAeNgL0BrPRADuenjBwBzNgBo4ACQAVNQAZbRRdAwA+OCkpOENDGKDQ8Mi